Z||000000||JBGehling||12-05-2000||09:06 PM||||Hey guys,<BR>  I was wondering some easy (not too expensive) ways to gain a little horsepower on Fieros. Like Hypertech chips (&lt;--- how much do they give you?)...etc.<P>Thanks<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000001||JBGehling||12-05-2000||10:53 PM||||...&lt;movin' on up&gt;...||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||12-05-2000||11:30 PM||||K&N drop in filter element and FLOWMASTER<BR>exhaust. period... about 300 bucks for both<BR>[keeping factery pipes, just replacing muffler] this will give you twice what a <BR>chip will give you in my opinion. then comes<BR>new plugs and wires. then if still not enough<BR>the chip for good measure, in that order. you<BR>just cant beat high air volume coming in and<BR>geting it out fast for h.p||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||12-06-2000||02:29 AM||||Some of the things I am doing to my 3.4L to help it breath easier:<P>Remove obstruction in stock airbox.  <BR>K&N drop in filter. ($20)<BR>Bored TB and Plenum  ($150)<BR>Gasket matching intakes <BR>Roller Rockers ($109) <BR>Remove obstructions from Exhaust Manifolds<BR>Undersized (Power) Pulley ($80)<BR>Accell Ignition Coil<P>I know that there is some question as to whether some of these things actually add any power, but I want to make sure that I am not robbing potential power that the engine has.||||reg||1
